      "title": "Setup required \u00b7 select models and a saved bundle",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Flux.2 Klein Base 4B \u00b7 use a saved RefMod\n\n1. Run RefMod_Bake_Image_Families.json first, with model=flux2 and the matching VAE.\n2. The loaders name the exact checkpoint variant, text encoder and VAE this preset targets. Install those files or their matching precision variants.\n3. In Image RefMod Apply, select flux2/example_character (or your own bundle). Model is auto (from refmod). Leaving the picker on None stops execution until a bundle is chosen. Refresh node definitions (R) after creating a bundle if it is not listed.\n4. Edit the prompt, then queue. References condition the result; identity, style and edit fidelity depend on the model and task.\n\n## Settings\n\nSampler values are starting points, not universal presets. Use the settings recommended for your exact checkpoint, especially for distilled models. Baked references must use the same VAE family as generation.\n\n## Native Flux.2 schedule\n\nFlux2Scheduler supplies the sigma schedule to SamplerCustomAdvanced. Its width and height must match the explicit Empty Flux 2 target (1024\u00d71024 initially). This graph targets Klein Base 4B: Qwen3-4B text encoder, Euler, 20 steps and CFG 5, matching ComfyUI's Base 4B edit template. CFG 1 disables classifier-free guidance and is not the Base preset. Distilled Klein and Flux.2 dev need their own model, text encoder and sampling settings. Use qwen_3_4b.safetensors for this setup; accepting another encoder's tensor dimensions does not verify the pairing.\n\nOptional: combine refmod_2/refmod_3 from the SAME family. ref_strength sets how long image references are active, not their pixel amplitude."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "# Flux.2 Klein Base 4B \u00b7 use a saved RefMod\n\n1. Run RefMod_Bake_Image_Families.json first, with model=flux2 and the matching VAE.\n2. The loaders name the exact checkpoint variant, text encoder and VAE this preset targets. Install those files or their matching precision variants.\n3. In Image RefMod Apply, select flux2/example_character (or your own bundle). Model is auto (from refmod). Leaving the picker on None stops execution until a bundle is chosen. Refresh node definitions (R) after creating a bundle if it is not listed.\n4. Edit the prompt, then queue. References condition the result; identity, style and edit fidelity depend on the model and task.\n\n## Settings\n\nSampler values are starting points, not universal presets. Use the settings recommended for your exact checkpoint, especially for distilled models. Baked references must use the same VAE family as generation.\n\n## Native Flux.2 schedule\n\nFlux2Scheduler supplies the sigma schedule to SamplerCustomAdvanced. Its width and height must match the explicit Empty Flux 2 target (1024\u00d71024 initially). This graph targets Klein Base 4B: Qwen3-4B text encoder, Euler, 20 steps and CFG 5, matching ComfyUI's Base 4B edit template. CFG 1 disables classifier-free guidance and is not the Base preset. Distilled Klein and Flux.2 dev need their own model, text encoder and sampling settings. Use qwen_3_4b.safetensors for this setup; accepting another encoder's tensor dimensions does not verify the pairing.\n\nOptional: combine refmod_2/refmod_3 from the SAME family. ref_strength sets how long image references are active, not their pixel amplitude."
      }
    },
